PVD("tonga_ndp_2011-2014",{"docs":["","TO Strategic Development Framework 2011 14"],"s":{"1":[[1,"11","5","Public Sector Management Reform Continuation","Continuing to implement public sector management reforms.",""],[1,"11","11","Prudent Budgeting and Public Financial Management Reform","Strategy 34: Ensuring a prudent budget based on available revenue and sustainable debt level, delivered through sound public financial management and quality government financial reporting.",""],[1,"11","14","Tax Reform and Modernisation Programme","Implementing tax reform and modernisation programmes to enhance revenue services and taxpayer's compliance.",""],[1,"15","1","Prudent Fiscal and Monetary Policy Maintenance","to maintain prudent fiscal and monetary policies, including undertaking careful reviews of expenditures and maintaining international good practices in budgeting, debt levels and financial management.",""],[1,"24","1","Legal, Judiciary, Electoral, and Security Administration Reforms","As part of these reforms government will consider related legal, judiciary and electoral reforms, international treaties, national security and administration improvements.",""],[1,"24","6","Judiciary Operations Strengthening","Strengthening the operation of the judiciary.",""],[1,"24","7","Justice, Police, and Defence Institutional Strengthening","the government, with aid from development partners, has strengthened the Ministry of Justice, Ministry of Police and Tonga Defence Services to improve their ability to respond appropriately to challenges and to enforce law and order.","Ministry of Justice | Ministry of Police | Tonga Defence Services"],[1,"37","4","Judiciary Operations Strengthening","Strengthening the operation of the judiciary.",""]],"2":[[1,"7","15","Public Enterprise Sustainability, Accountability, and Privatization Reform","Ensuring Public Enterprises are sustainable and accountable, and where appropriate moved into the private sector.",""],[1,"11","7","Private Sector Function Transfer Reform","Strategy 32: Transferring a range of functions to the private sector.",""],[1,"11","18","Public Enterprise Reform","Continuing to implement public enterprise reform.",""],[1,"11","19","Public Enterprise Privatization Policy","Privatising public enterprises where appropriate.",""],[1,"26","2","Public Sector Service Transfer and Privatization Reform","it is envisaged that a number of services now performed by the public sector will be moved either directly to the private sector, via outsourcing, public-private partnerships (PPP), and privatisation; or by taking the intermediate step of transferring them first to Public Enterprise status.",""],[1,"26","3","Private Sector Consultative Mechanism for Outsourcing and Privatization","government will establish a consultative mechanism with the private sector on ways to facilitate this.",""],[1,"29","3","Public Enterprise Performance Improvement","Improving profitability, accountability, and return on equity of public enterprises.",""],[1,"29","4","Public Enterprise Reform Programme","Continuing to implement public enterprise reforms.",""],[1,"29","5","Public Enterprise Privatization","Privatising public enterprises where appropriate.",""],[1,"29","6","Public Enterprise Management Improvement Measures","Government will continue to seek ways to promote more efficient management of PE through training and performance incentives, associated with closer monitoring.",""],[1,"29","7","Public Enterprise Reform and Efficiency Improvement","the government, in cooperation with international partners, is also evaluating ways to improve the efficiency and accountability of its existing PEs.",""],[1,"29","7","Public Enterprise Reform Acceleration Measures","the government will seek to accelerate the reform of PEs, taking appropriate measures for each enterprise based on careful analysis of benefits and costs.",""],[1,"29","8","Public Enterprise Function Review and Ownership Restructuring","Government will review the functions of all the PEs to decide which ones might best continue with majority government shareholding to meet national objectives, and which ones can be partially or fully sold off to the private sector.",""],[1,"29","8","Transparent Subsidy Support for Public Enterprises with Social Functions","Where government requires a PE to provide a specific social function, which has negative commercial consequences, Government will ensure a clear and transparent subsidy is provided.",""],[1,"38","15","Public Enterprises Reform","Continuing to implement public enterprises reform.",""],[1,"38","17","Public Enterprise Privatization Policy","Privatizing public enterprises where appropriate.",""]],"3":[[1,"10","4","Health Services Network Maintenance and Improvement","Maintaining and improving the network of health services delivered through the national referral hospital at Vaiola, supported by a network of regional hospitals and community clinics, to deliver effective curative and preventative health care.",""],[1,"21","4","National Health Services Network Maintenance and Improvement","Maintaining and improving the network of health services delivered through the national referral hospital at Vaiola, supported by a network of regional hospitals and community clinics, to deliver effective curative and preventative health care.",""],[1,"21","5","Preventive Health Care Programme Improvement","Improving efficiency and effectiveness of preventative health care programmes that encourage healthy life styles, including consumption of appropriate foods and increased exercise, so as to decrease the incidence of non-communicable diseases.",""],[1,"21","6","Health Services Maintenance and Improvement Programme","Ministry of Health (MOH) is focussed on maintaining and improving the delivery of health services through the national referral hospital at Vaiola, supported by a network of regional hospitals and community clinics, to deliver effective curative and preventative health care, guided by the principles of health systems strengthening based on Primary Health Care values.","Ministry of Health (MOH)"],[1,"21","8","Health Service Improvement and Preventive Primary Health Care Programme","Government will improve the provision of health services across Tonga, with continued emphasis on preventative health care focusing on non-communicable diseases, rather than on curative medicine alone.","MOH"],[1,"21","8","Preventive Health Programme Efficiency and Effectiveness Improvement","The efficiency and effectiveness of the preventative health care programmes of the MOH will be improved to encouraging healthy life styles, with greater emphasis on reduction of the main NCD Risk Factors such as tobacco smoking, alcohol misuse, physical inactivity and unhealthy eating; in order to decrease the incidence of non-communicable disease.","MOH"],[1,"36","3","National Health Services Network Maintenance and Improvement","Maintaining and improving the net work of health services delivered through the national referral hospital at Vaiola, supported by a network of regional hospitals and community clinics, to deliver effective curative and preventative health care.",""],[1,"36","6","Preventive Health Care Improvement Programme","Improving efficiency and effectiveness of preventative health care programs that encourage healthy lifestyles, consumption of appropriate foods and increased exercise, so as to decrease the incidence of non-communicable diseases.",""],[1,"40","7","Non-Communicable Disease Reduction Priority","our urgent priority is the reduction in prevalence and impact of non-communicable diseases.",""]],"4":[[1,"9","3","Safe and Reliable Transport Infrastructure Development and Maintenance","Ensuring safe and reliable transport infrastructure (roads, ports, airports), with the necessary institutional arrangements in place to manage and fund effective development and maintenance of these facilities throughout the Kingdom.",""],[1,"16","4","Improve Access to International Shipping","Government will also focus on improving access to international shipping to help keep down transport costs.",""],[1,"18","6","Safe and Reliable Transport Infrastructure Development and Maintenance","Ensuring safe and reliable transport infrastructure (roads, ports, airports), with the necessary institutional arrangements in place to manage and fund effective development and maintenance of these facilities throughout the Kingdom.",""],[1,"18","8","Transport Sector Regulatory Compliance and Safety Oversight","Strengthening regulatory compliance and safety oversight of transport sector to ensure compliance with international safety standards.",""],[1,"19","4","Infrastructure Modernisation and Regulatory Enforcement","Government will continue to strengthen and modernise infrastructure to reduce business costs and to facilitate market access for a thriving and successful economy.",""],[1,"19","6","Sustainable and Affordable Outer Islands Transport Links","The government will focus on promoting sustainable and affordable transport links from the aviation and maritime industries, while ensuring safe and reliable operation of these transport services.",""],[1,"33","38","Safe and Reliable Transport Infrastructure Development","Ensuring safe and reliable transport infrastructure (roads, ports, airports), with the necessary institutional arrangements in place to manage and fund effective development and",""],[1,"34","7","Transport Sector Regulatory Compliance and Safety Oversight","Strengthening regulatory compliance and safety oversight of the transport sector to ensure compliance with international safety standard.",""]],"5":[[1,"5","3","Strategic Planning Guidance for Sector and Ministry Plans","Guide the further formulation of the sector development plans, ministries' corporate and annual management plans and the annual budgets through which resources are allocated",""],[1,"6","3","Monitoring and Evaluation Structure","Chapter 2 outlines the process for establishing a Monitoring and Evaluation structure to allow us to track progress against each strategy leading up to our objectives and vision.",""],[1,"6","3","Sector Plan and Corporate Plan Monitoring and Evaluation","This structure will be complemented by the more detailed monitoring and evaluation of the sector plans, Ministries Annual Management and longer term Corporate Plans, and the annual budgets.",""],[1,"19","3","National Infrastructure Investment Plan","a National Infrastructure Investment Plan (NIIP) was approved in November 2010.",""],[1,"25","6","Programme-Based Budgeting and Performance Management Reform","government ministries will continue to embrace this shift, increasing their adaptation of programme-based budgeting and matching resources to services in order to better serve the people throughout the Kingdom.",""],[1,"25","8","Review of Ministry Corporate and Annual Management Plans","Ministries' Corporate and Annual Management Plans will be reviewed to determine their applicability to national development objectives; it will mean scaling back or the elimination of programmes that do not serve this purpose.",""],[1,"26","1","Corporate and Annual Management Planning Reform","Corporate Plans and Annual Management Plans will be articulated with concrete goals and outputs to address the core functions and areas of responsibility of each ministry or agency in the TSDF.",""],[1,"26","1","Budget Linkage and Performance Monitoring Reform","These plans will be reviewed regularly to ensure that the budget is linked to concrete goals and outputs, and monitored to ensure they are being delivered.",""],[1,"27","2","Ministry Expenditure Review and Reallocation","the government will institute a thorough review of all ministry expenditure to identify activities and programmes of low priority that can be cut and resources reallocated to higher priority areas.",""],[1,"27","4","More Frequent Budget Reporting for Budget Monitoring","more frequent budget reports to help monitor budget execution in a more effective and timely manner, to facilitate early identification and correction of any divergences from the approved budget during the year",""],[1,"27","10","Prioritized and Costed Annual Ministry Plans","encouraging line ministries to produce prioritised and costed AMPs;",""],[1,"28","1","Line Ministry Budget Alignment and AMP Revision Requirement","ensuring that line ministries receive budget allocations sufficient to cover their basic expenditure obligations; and requiring line ministries to amend their AMP subsequent to the finalisation of the budget in order to ensure that planned activities are consistent with budget appropriations",""],[1,"28","3","Chart of Accounts Revision and Budget Sub-program Monitoring","completing the revision to the chart of accounts which has eliminated redundant and duplicate codes, improve clarity and increase uniformity, and has prepared for the shift to sub-program level allocation and monitoring of budgets",""],[1,"28","6","Public Resource Priority-Setting Policy and Decision-Making Framework","setting clear policies and having effective decision making process in place for setting priorities among competing uses of public resources",""],[1,"31","2","Simple First Steps for Improved Monitoring and Evaluation","Recognizing the importance of M&E, but also the danger of creating an overly burdensome system that interferes with implementation, some simple first steps for improved M&E is set out in this chapter.",""],[1,"31","2","Expanded Monitoring and Evaluation System Development","With experience, this will be developed further during the period of the TSDF to ensure it meets the needs of Tonga.",""],[1,"31","3","Monitoring and Evaluation Results Use for Planning and Budgeting","The results of the M&E will be used for the Ministries' Annual Reports, and for updating their next year AMP and justification for their next budget bid.",""],[1,"31","3","Progress Tracking and Strategy Adjustment Mechanism","It will also be used to track progress towards our Outcome Objectives and identify areas where we need to modify our strategies and Ministry Plans in light of new challenges and other developments.",""],[1,"32","1","M&E System Operationalization and Data Quality Strengthening","making the M&E system operational will be to strengthen the accuracy and reliability of necessary information.",""],[1,"32","2","Corporate Plan and Annual Management Plan Review and Alignment","The Policy and Planning Division of the Ministry of Finance and National Planning is tasked to review these corporate plans and the associated annual management plans to ensure alignment to the key outcome objectives, the annual budget and the achievement of the targets for each indicator.","Ministry of Finance and National Planning"],[1,"32","2","Revised Planning and Budgeting System Support","The MoFNP is also available to assist Ministries with the implementation of this revised planning and budgeting system and the associated monitoring and evaluation.","MoFNP"],[1,"32","4","Monitoring Matrix Development for Ministries","During the first year of the TSDF period, the Policy and Planning Division, MoFNP will help Ministries to convert the table into a simple monitoring matrix with indicators and targets that are fully consistent with the SMART criteria, and with a base line.","Policy and Planning Division, MoFNP | Ministries"],[1,"32","4","Development of New Data Series","This will require an open dialogue based on what is available and, where considered appropriate, the development of new data series, in consultation with the Statistics Department, may be required.","Statistics Department"],[1,"40","7","Data Gap Closure Efforts","we are making efforts at closing some data gaps.",""],[1,"42","3","Results-Based Public Expenditure Prioritization","Given the limited resources available over the next two years the focus will be on the application of funds to produce outcomes and outputs that are of value to government and the community.",""],[1,"42","3","National Outcome-Based Planning Framework","The TSDF has specified nine national outcome objectives whereby line ministries must produce outputs that contribute to their achievements.","line ministries"]],"6":[[1,"5","5","External Economic Relations and Development Partnership Framework","Provide the foundation on which the government can develop its external economic relations and development partners can construct their country strategies and assistance programmes in a spirit of true partnership",""],[1,"7","16","Whole-of-Government Coordination with Development Partners","Ensuring a more coordinated whole of government approach in Tonga's partnership with development partners.",""],[1,"29","11","Aid Principles and Management Strategy","the government has recently established and agreed with development partners an Aid Principles and Management Strategy to guide this partnership.",""],[1,"29","11","Aid and Project Management Division Review Requirement","These rules require that all donor applications over an agreed amount go through the Aid and Project Management Division of the Ministry of Finance and National Planning.","Ministry of Finance and National Planning"],[1,"30","1","Development Partner Coordination Forums","Overall coordination and harmonisation will continue to be enhanced by regular Tonga Development Partner Forums in addition to regular bilateral programming meetings.",""],[1,"30","5","Support for Regional Governance and Aid Effectiveness Frameworks","Tonga also supports the Pacific Plan, and attempts to adhere to the Forum Principles of Good Governance and Accountability, to the Paris Declaration and Pacific Principles of Aid Effectiveness and to the Cairns Compact.",""],[1,"30","5","Participation in Peacekeeping Activities","The Tongan Defence Services also engages with a number of peace keeping activities around the world.",""],[1,"30","5","Participation in Regional and International Meetings","Through its participation in regional and international meetings Tonga will continue to play a responsible role in furthering the interests of Tonga as well as the Pacific region as a whole.",""]],"7":[[1,"7","7","Technical and Vocational Education and Training Improvement","by delivering improved Technical and Vocational Education and Training.",""],[1,"8","7","Youth Development Programmes","by promoting youth development programmes, including community economic development and consideration of a National Youth Service.",""],[1,"9","14","Technical and Vocational Education and Training Improvement","Appropriately skilled workforce to meet the available opportunities in Tonga and overseas, by delivering improved Technical and Vocational Education and Training.",""],[1,"14","1","Youth Development Programmes","by promoting youth development programmes, including community economic development and the consideration of a National Youth Service.",""],[1,"14","3","Youth Income Generation and Commercial Activities Support","The Ministry of Training, Employment, Youth and Sports is encouraging participation in income generation and commercial activities to help these groups, in particular youths, to develop skills and meet their basic economic needs.","Ministry of Training, Employment, Youth and Sports"],[1,"14","3","Community-Based Rural Youth Tourism Employment Initiative","Tourism, in particular community based, also provides youth in rural communities with new employment opportunities and roles where service sector business skills can be developed.",""],[1,"15","3","Workforce Development and Training Investment","Investing in a healthy, well-educated, and skilled workforce.",""],[1,"15","3","Development Training for Business Value Addition","Directing development training to increase the value-added of business.",""],[1,"15","4","Support for Primary Education and Vocational Training","the government will continue to support both primary education and vocational training.",""],[1,"15","5","Business Training and Advisory Support","The government will also utilise local businesses and organisations for broader business training, advisory training for businesses/private sector and continue its cooperation with international organisations willing to impart business knowledge.",""],[1,"20","4","School-Based Vocational Education Expansion","the expansion of school- based vocational education",""],[1,"20","7","Domestic Training Institution Development and External Training Mobilization","Promoting skill development through appropriate development of domestic training institutions, and mobilisation of external training opportunities.",""],[1,"20","8","Education and Training Productivity Alignment Initiative","Improving the focus of education and training on increased productivity of the work force to increase production, exports and overseas employment of Tongans.",""],[1,"20","9","Technical and Vocational Education and Training Development","Particular attention will be given to the development of technical vocational education and training at the post-basic education level.",""],[1,"20","9","TVET Integration in Upper Secondary Schools","Efforts will also be made to introduce TVET as part of the options and subjects taught at the upper levels of secondary schools to prepare students for post-secondary TVET training.",""],[1,"20","9","TVET Expansion to Outer Islands and Rural Areas","This will be extended to the outer islands and rural areas through developing partnerships and collaborations with the churches and NGOs.",""],[1,"21","1","TVET Reform and International Re-alignment","TVET will be reformed and re-aligned with international requirements and standards.",""],[1,"21","2","TVET Alignment for International Labour Market Access","TVET will be designed to facilitate access to those opportunities.",""],[1,"21","2","TVET International Accreditation and Recognition Initiative","Work will be done to ensure international accreditation and recognition of TVET in Tonga as well as in other countries.",""],[1,"21","3","Community Informal Skills Training Frameworks and Programmes","At the community level, informal training will be institutionalised into training frameworks and training programmes",""],[1,"35","20","Education and Training Productivity Alignment Initiative","Improving the focus of education and training on increased productivity of the work force to increase production, exports and overseas employment of Tongans.",""],[1,"40","7","Secondary and Vocational Education Improvement","we are looking to address other challenges in secondary and vocational education.",""]],"8":[[1,"9","12","Primary Education Provision and Secondary Education Partnership","Continuing to focus on government provision of primary education, working in partnership with the churches and other groups for the provision of secondary education.",""],[1,"9","13","Universal Basic Education Support and Improvement","Supporting and improving universal basic education through the implementation of the education sector strategy.",""],[1,"9","17","Domestic Training Institution Development and External Training Mobilization","Promoting skill development through appropriate development of domestic training institutions, and mobilisation of external training opportunities.",""],[1,"9","18","Education and Training Productivity Alignment Strategy","Strategy 18: Improving the focus of education and training on increased productivity of the work force to increase production, exports and overseas employment of Tongans.",""],[1,"20","2","Primary Education Provision and Secondary Education Partnership","Continuing to focus on government provision of primary education, working in partnership with the churches and other groups for the provision of secondary education.",""],[1,"20","3","Education Sector Strategy Implementation for Universal Basic Education","Supporting and improving universal basic education through the implementation of the education sector strategy.",""],[1,"20","4","Support for Government and Non-Government School Partnership","government will continue to support this partnership to reduce inequalities with non-government-run schools",""],[1,"20","4","Universal Basic Education Quality Improvement","focussing attention on supporting and improving quality universal basic education",""],[1,"20","4","Education System Reform and Compulsory Schooling Extension","the major reform of the education system, extension of compulsory education to eighteen years",""],[1,"20","5","National Curriculum Revamp for Basic Education","The national curriculum for basic education is currently being revamped to ensure a balance between academic, skill and vocational training.",""],[1,"20","5","Alternative Learning Pathways Programme","Programmes will be developed to provide alternative pathways for students with different learning needs, whether for the 4 to 18 year age group, or post- 18, these must still be based on a sound basic education, which will provide the necessary tools and attributes for further learning.",""],[1,"20","5","Education Plan Implementation","Government will continue with the implementation of the Education Plan.",""],[1,"22","4","Tongan Cultural Activities in the National Curriculum","Government will consider reintroducing a greater focus on Tongan cultural activities within the national curriculum",""],[1,"35","1","Primary Education Provision and Secondary Education Partnership","Continuing to focus on government provision of primary education, working in partnership with the churches and other groups for the provision of secondary education.",""],[1,"35","4","Universal Basic Education Support and Improvement","Supporting and improving universal basic education through the implementation of the education sector strategy.",""]],"9":[[1,"9","7","Reliable and Cost-Efficient Power Supply Expansion","Maintaining and where possible expanding the provision of reliable and cost efficient power supplies, using traditional and renewable options, to all communities.",""],[1,"18","10","Reliable and Cost-Efficient Power Supply Expansion","Maintaining and where possible expanding, the provision of reliable and cost efficient power supplies, using traditional and renewable options, to all communities.",""],[1,"19","7","Fuel Procurement and Supply Chain Efficiency Measures","Government will seek options with the fuel industry for more cost effective procurement, shipment, delivery, storage and distribution of fuel.",""],[1,"19","7","Tonga Energy Road Map","The Tonga Energy Road Map (TERM) has been developed to help achieve energy security through reducing reliance on imported petroleum.",""],[1,"19","7","Renewable Energy Target Achievement","Government will work toward achieving the national target of 50% renewable energy, originally set for 2012, as part of government's commitment to cutting costs and addressing climate change.",""],[1,"34","16","Reliable and Cost-Efficient Power Supply Expansion","Maintaining and where possible expanding the provision of reliable and cost efficient power supplies, using traditional and renewable options, to all communities.",""]],"10":[[1,"9","8","Safe Waste Collection, Disposal, and Recycling Expansion","Improving and where possible expanding the safe collection, disposal and recycling of solid and liquid waste to protect people's health and the environment.",""],[1,"18","11","Safe Waste Collection, Disposal, and Recycling Expansion","Improving, and where possible expanding, the safe collection, disposal and recycling of solid and liquid waste to protect people's health and the environment.",""],[1,"18","12","Safe Water and Sanitation Access Expansion","Maintaining and expanding access to safe water and sanitation for all communities.",""],[1,"19","8","Priority Water and Sanitation Projects","Government and relevant agencies will also maintain and expand access to safe water and sanitation for all communities through implementing the proposed priority water and sanitation projects outlined in the NIIP and other related programs.",""],[1,"19","8","Enforcement of Water and Sanitation Legislation","The strong and active enforcement of the existing legislative Acts related to water and sanitation, are very important for the sustainable management of water resources and standard of sanitation in Tonga as a whole.",""],[1,"20","1","Modern Waste Handling, Disposal and Recycling Improvement","Government will work with communities and business to improve the handling, disposal and recycling of such waste to avoid damaging the environment, and where possible find productive uses for the waste.",""],[1,"34","19","Safe Waste Collection, Disposal, and Recycling Expansion","Improving and where possible expanding the safe collection, disposal and recycling of solid and liquid waste to protect people's health and the environment.",""],[1,"34","19","Safe Water and Sanitation Access Expansion","Maintaining and expanding access to safe water and sanitation for all communities.",""]],"11":[[1,"10","10","Environmental Impact Assessment Enforcement and Environmental Management Capacity Strengthening","Strategy 22: Ensuring sustainable use of the environment, by enforcing Environmental Impact Assessments (EIAs), and strengthen the national capability for environmental management to create incentives for limiting the use of resources and production of waste.",""],[1,"17","6","Sustainable Fisheries Development and Management","Through the Fisheries Division of MAFFF, government will work towards ensuring sustainable development and management of off-shore and inshore aquatic resources with particular focus on tuna and long-line fisheries, DWL fishing, sport fishing and aquarium fishery.","Fisheries Division of MAFFF"],[1,"17","7","Fisheries Research, Regulation, and Surveillance Services","Fisheries Division will continue to carry out a range of public services including research and extension, monitoring and regulation of vessels and fishing activities, monitoring of fish catches and sales, and surveillance of the exclusive economic zone to control illegal fishing.",""],[1,"17","7","Fish Stock Research and Licensing Enforcement","Emphasis will also be placed on better research on stock levels and enforcement of licences to ensure sustainable use of these resources and avoid similar export boom and busts as experienced with products like sea- cucumbers.",""],[1,"18","2","Mineral Wealth Legislation Review","Government will review the need for new legislation to ensure that exploration and any future mining or extraction of resources will generate a significant benefit to the Kingdom.",""],[1,"22","6","Environmental Impact Assessment Enforcement and Environmental Management Capacity Strengthening","Ensuring sustainable use of the environment, by enforcing Environmental Impact Assessments (EIAs), and strengthen the national capability for environmental management to create incentives for limiting the use of resources and production of waste.",""],[1,"22","7","Environmental Impact Assessment Enforcement","The government is committed to ensure sustainable development by enforcing Environmental Impact Assessments (EIAs), strengthening the national capability for environmental management and also integrating sustainable development into all of its policies and budgetary processes.",""],[1,"22","7","National Environmental Management Capacity Strengthening","The government is committed to ensure sustainable development by enforcing Environmental Impact Assessments (EIAs), strengthening the national capability for environmental management and also integrating sustainable development into all of its policies and budgetary processes.",""],[1,"22","7","Sustainable Development Mainstreaming in Policy and Budgeting","The government is committed to ensure sustainable development by enforcing Environmental Impact Assessments (EIAs), strengthening the national capability for environmental management and also integrating sustainable development into all of its policies and budgetary processes.",""],[1,"22","7","Land and Sea Use Knowledge Improvement Initiative","A better understanding of the factors affecting land and sea-use will be sought to ensure sustainable use of these resources to contribute to appropriate fisheries, agriculture and tourism development which depend on a quality environment.",""],[1,"22","8","Resilience and Resource Management Options Study","Government will explore options for enhancing the resilience of government, communities, businesses and natural resources; exploring the environmental, economic and societal consequences of changes in the demands on and availability of freshwater and other resources.",""],[1,"22","8","Sustainable Resource Use Incentive Policy","A strong focus will be placed on improved management of resources to ensure sustainable use both for domestic use and promoting exports by creating incentives for limiting the use of resources and production of waste.",""],[1,"22","8","Climate Change Mitigation and Adaptation Analysis","Greater effort will be made to analyse the options, risks and uncertainties in mitigating and adapting to climate change and variability.",""],[1,"23","1","Environmental Legislation, Policy, and Enforcement Strengthening","Government will strengthen legislation, policies and enforcement with regards to the environment and its natural resources.",""],[1,"23","1","Environmental Impact Assessment Regulation Enforcement","the government will strive to fully enforce regulations such as the approved Environment Impact Assessment (EIA) Regulation.",""],[1,"36","8","Mainstreaming Procedures and Consultation Mechanisms","Cultural awareness, environmental sustainability, disaster risk management and climate change adaptation, integrated into all planning and implementation of programs, by establishing and adhering to appropriate procedures and consultation mechanisms.",""],[1,"40","7","Ministry of Environment and Climate Change","through our new Ministry of Environment and Climate Change,","Ministry of Environment and Climate Change"]],"12":[[1,"10","6","Integration of Sustainability and Risk Management Procedures","Cultural awareness, environmental sustainability, disaster risk management and climate change adaptation, integrated into all planning and implementation of programmes, by establishing and adhering to appropriate procedures and consultation mechanisms.",""],[1,"10","11","Implementation of the JNAP-CCADRM","Strategy 23: Implementing the JNAP-CCADRM to reduce vulnerability & risks; and to enhance resilience to the impacts of climate change & natural hazards.",""],[1,"23","2","National Disaster Risk Management Mainstreaming and JNAP-CCADRM Implementation","The Ministry of Works, in collaboration with Ministry of Environment and Climate Change, is responsible for compliance with the National Emergency Management Act, Implementation of National Disaster Plan and mainstreaming Disaster Risk Management through a Joint National Action Plan on Climate Change Adaptation and Disaster Risk Management (JNAP-CCADRM).","Ministry of Works | Ministry of Environment and Climate Change"],[1,"23","3","Implementation of the Pacific Disaster Risk Reduction Management Framework for Action","Government is also supporting the implementation of the Pacific Disaster Risk Reduction Management Framework for Action, 2005 - 2015.",""],[1,"23","3","Tonga JNAP-CCADRM Implementation","Government will implement Tonga's JNAP- CCADRM focussing on improving disaster mitigation through better design and placement of infrastructure and improved evacuation planning for communities.",""],[1,"23","3","Disaster Response and Recovery Capacity Development","Improved response, to disasters when they happen, will also be developed to help communities to recover more quickly.",""],[1,"23","4","Multi-Hazards Risk Management Framework","Government will seek to develop a framework for multi-hazards risk management that will improve infrastructure investments and contribute to the development of sustainable communities in Tonga.",""],[1,"23","5","International Climate Action Advocacy and Adaptation Support","Government will continue to take an active role in encouraging the international community to take the global actions needed to address human driven climate change and where mitigation is not possible, find suitable options for adaptation.",""],[1,"36","22","Implementation of the JNAP-CCADRM","Implementing the JNAP-CCADRM to reduce vulnerability & risks; and to enhance resilience to the impacts of climate change & natural hazards.",""]],"13":[[1,"7","4","Public-Private Partnership Promotion Framework","Dynamic public and private sector partnership as the engine of growth, by promoting better collaboration between government and business, appropriate incentives and streamlining of rules and regulations.",""],[1,"8","8","Public-Private Partnership for Growth","Dynamic public and private sector partnership as the engine of growth, by promoting better collaboration between government and business, appropriate incentives, and streamlining of rules and regulations",""],[1,"8","16","Private Sector Engagement in Policy Formulation and Implementation","(vi) Involving the private sector more closely in policy formulation and implementation",""],[1,"14","6","Public-Private Partnership for Economic Restructuring","Within the framework of economic restructuring the public and private sectors must work closely together in a partnership that will create the engine of growth to generate the necessary employment and income for the people, and which will in turn generate revenue to pay for the operation of government.",""],[1,"14","8","Private Sector Policy Stability and Transparency Measures","To avoid these undesirable effects, the government, in conjunction with NRBT, will continue",""],[1,"15","7","Private Sector Participation in Policy Formulation and Implementation","Involving the private sector more closely in policy formulation and implementation.",""],[1,"15","8","Private Sector Consultation and Regulatory Reform Mechanism","The government resolves to continue and further improve its successful public consultations regarding policies impacting on business, as well as continuing successful public/private institutions such as the Task Force on Regulatory Reform and its Working Groups.",""],[1,"15","12","Policy Response Capacity and Regulatory Reform for Business Environment","improve effective policy response capacity of Government to ensure stable business environment, relevance of regulations, promote fair competition, investment and development markets to restore integrity to the business community",""],[1,"15","13","Corporate Registration and Business Credit Facilitation","promoting registration of corporate bodies and facilitating business and consumer credit to secure and increase private sector growth",""],[1,"16","2","Foreign Investment and Foreign Business Promotion","the government will continue to encourage foreign investment and the opening of foreign businesses in the country to complement those established by domestic investors.",""],[1,"16","4","Tonga Trade and Investment Board","To facilitate such access, Government will establish the Tonga Trade and Investment Board.",""],[1,"22","5","Culturally Sensitive Business Development Promotion","Where possible, the development of new business opportunities, such as appropriate Tourism, will be used to encourage the strengthening of our cultural traditions.",""],[1,"25","3","Business Licensing Regime Review and Reform","the government will carefully examine the current business licensing regime and remove obstacles to business while at the same time better safeguarding the health and safety of employees.",""],[1,"25","3","Investment and Licensing Legislation Review","The legislation governing investment and licensing will also be reviewed for effectiveness, and government agencies will be required to consider the impact of new regulations on business before measures are enacted.",""],[1,"25","4","Review of Competent Authority Price-Setting Role","The role of the Competent Authority, in setting sensitive prices, will be reviewed to ensure it is effective without placing unnecessary constraints on business.",""],[1,"25","4","Task Force on Regulatory Reform","the government will continue to pursue institutional avenues for change, through the Task Force on Regulatory Reform and through the encouragement of private sector participation in legal and regulatory commercial reforms.",""],[1,"25","4","Private Sector Participation in Legal and Regulatory Commercial Reforms","the government will continue to pursue institutional avenues for change, through the Task Force on Regulatory Reform and through the encouragement of private sector participation in legal and regulatory commercial reforms.",""],[1,"33","24","Private Sector Engagement in Policy Formulation and Implementation","(vi) Involving the private sector more closely in policy formulation and implementation.",""],[1,"37","10","Legal and Regulatory Reform for an Enabling Environment","Ensuring a conducive enabling environment through legal and regulatory reform.",""],[1,"39","7","Economic Reform Programme to Open Investment","The government is meeting these challenges by developing and implementing a reform programme to raise economic performance.",""],[1,"42","1","Private Sector Investment Promotion","There is a need to make Tonga a more attractive destination for increased levels of private sector investment that will lead to employment creation and provide other livelihood opportunities.",""],[1,"42","6","Inclusive Growth Promotion Strategy","Government will focus on promoting wider more inclusive growth which will generate benefits more widely through the Kingdom.",""]],"14":[[1,"26","4","Government ICT Service Delivery and Public Communication Strategy","The government is committed to develop a communication strategy to increase the amount of information available on its existing websites, creating new websites for ministries and agencies where not currently available, and creating interfaces for the public in areas such as business licensing, procurement, trade and social services.",""],[1,"26","4","ICT-Based Public Consultation and Outer Islands Internet Access Improvement","The government will also solicit consultation with the public via ICT, as well as seek to improve the ability of outer islands to utilise the internet to communicate with government.",""],[1,"26","5","Fibre-Optic Cable Link Project","A major project for a fibre-optic cable link to improve band-width and internet connectivity is now well-advanced;",""],[1,"34","12","Information and Communications Sector Performance Improvement","Improving the performance of the information and communications sector, with quality service delivery, free and fair availability of information, geographical coverage, service affordability and access to new service applications.",""],[1,"37","18","ICT for Accountability and Transparency Initiative","Utilizing Information and Communication Technology (ICT) to improve accountability and transparency.",""]],"15":[[1,"7","13","Government Efficiency and Coordination Improvement","Continuing progress to a more efficient and effective government by focussing on its core functions; improving coordination, service delivery and optimising use of resources.",""],[1,"11","1","Government Efficiency and Coordination Improvement","Continuing progress to a more efficient and effective government by focussing on its core functions; improving coordination, service delivery and optimising use of resources.",""],[1,"13","2","Functional and Responsive Government Systems Development","The Framework will focus on developing appropriately functional government systems at all levels (outer islands, district, and town/village), that are consultative and responsive to the needs of communities.",""]],"16":[[1,"8","6","Institutional Care and Support Services Expansion","Strategy 3: Increasing institutional care and support services for the elderly and other vulnerable groups, including investigation of the potential private sector role.",""],[1,"13","5","Local Institution Support for Rural Services and Vulnerable Groups","Government will ensure local institutions have the resources to protect and develop rural services, with a particular focus on the needs of the vulnerable.",""]],"17":[[1,"18","3","Diaspora Engagement and Remittance Mobilization","Efforts will be made to retain the close cultural and social relations with Tongans who have established residence overseas to maintain remittances and opportunities for them to invest in and provide technical skills to Tonga.",""]],"18":[[1,"8","7","Community Economic Development Initiative","by promoting youth development programmes, including community economic development and consideration of a National Youth Service.",""],[1,"13","2","Community Empowerment and Self-Reliance Initiative","The aim will be to empower communities and build more self-reliance at all levels to address community development needs.",""],[1,"13","4","Gender-Balanced Economic Opportunities and Skills Training Programme","This will be achieved by promoting skills, enterprises and innovation through training men, women and youths at the community level and in the informal sectors.",""],[1,"13","4","Inclusive Product Development and Craftsmanship Training Initiative","In addition, efforts will be made through training interventions to encourage product development, creativity and craftsmanship, while paying attention to gender-specific needs.",""],[1,"14","5","Informal Sector Support and Gradual Formalization","This will be addressed in the support to the private sector, which will include finding ways to gradually integrate the informal sector into the more formal sector.",""],[1,"14","5","Cooperative Strengthening and Small-Scale Credit Access","Improved cooperatives and access to small scale credit for these informal sectors is important for their development.",""],[1,"14","6","Business Start-up and Lawful Commerce Support","Supporting Tongans and foreign investors to open businesses and engage in lawful commerce is a key of element of the government's programme.",""],[1,"15","2","Financial Sector Development and Inclusion Support","The government will support the continued development of both traditional financial sector institutions and their pursuit of better risk management, as well as the development of non-bank financial institutions.",""],[1,"15","2","Microfinance and Financial Inclusion Expansion","The government will also focus on the development of microfinance and financial inclusion, targeting those who are presently not well served by the existing financial system.",""]],"19":[[1,"16","5","Trade Liberalisation and Overseas Employment Expansion","Government will continue to liberalise trade policy, and seek opportunities for overseas employment.",""],[1,"16","5","Seasonal and Temporary Worker Mobility Schemes","This will include the \"recognised seasonal employers\" scheme in New Zealand and similar temporary worker schemes in Australia and USA.",""],[1,"16","6","Active Membership in International and Regional Trade Bodies","This will include continuing its active membership in international and regional trade bodies such as the World Trade Organisation (WTO) and the Pacific Island Countries Trade Agreement (PICTA).",""],[1,"16","7","Non-Tariff Barrier Removal and Tariff Liberalization","Regional trade will be encouraged by the elimination of non-tariff barriers in the short term and progressively removing all tariff barriers over a longer period, to be replaced by alternative revenue raising options.",""],[1,"16","7","PACER Membership Negotiation Preparation","Establishing the foundation for negotiating membership in the Pacific Agreement on Closer Economic Relations (PACER) is underway.",""],[1,"16","8","Economic Partnership Agreement Finalisation","Finally, through the Pacific Islands Forum and in concert with African, Caribbean, and Pacific Island (ACP) countries, the government will finalise an Economic Partnership Agreement (EPA) with the European Union (EU).",""],[1,"16","8","Trade, Investment, Fisheries, and Development Assistance Agreement Package","The EPA is expected to comprise a master agreement aimed at enhancing the trading and investment-attracting capacity of ACP states, and subsidiary agreements covering trade in goods and services (including tourism), investment and fisheries and development assistance.",""],[1,"16","9","National Export Strategy","A National Export Strategy (NES) will be formulated and implemented over the life of this framework, based on Tonga's comparative advantages, addressing constraints and forging a closer and realistic partnership between government and private sector businesses.",""],[1,"18","4","Overseas Labour Mobility Access Negotiation","The government will continue to negotiate with Australia and New Zealand for improved access to their overseas labour mobility schemes, and will seek similar options in the US.",""],[1,"18","4","Overseas Labour Mobility Arrangement Management","Government will ensure that such arrangements are managed effectively and responsibility so that these opportunities may continue in the long run.",""]],"20":[[1,"10","1","Healthy Lifestyle and Non-Communicable Disease Prevention Initiative","Improved health of the people, by promoting healthy lifestyle choices with particular focus on addressing non-communicable diseases, and providing quality, effective and sustainable health services.",""],[1,"10","5","Preventive Health Care Programme Improvement","Strategy 20: Improving efficiency and effectiveness of preventative health care programmes that encourage healthy life styles, including consumption of appropriate foods and increased exercise, so as to decrease the incidence of non-communicable diseases.",""],[1,"15","5","Health Lifestyle Promotion Programme","The health programme will continue to promote a healthier life style thereby reducing work-time lost through illness and raising productivity.",""]],"21":[[1,"8","5","Gender Equality Policy Implementation","Strategy 2: Improving gender equality by implementing the government's gender development policy.",""]],"22":[[1,"8","4","Outer Island and Rural Development Programme Formulation and Implementation through Local Communities","Strategy 1: Better formulation and implementation of outer island and rural development programmes through local communities.",""],[1,"12","5","Outer Islands and Rural Development Programmes","Government believes that all parts of the country should enjoy similar economic and social opportunities, enabling the outer islands and rural development programmes to contribute to national prosperity.",""],[1,"12","5","Community Development Initiative","Community development is at the core of this strategic framework and will support many of the other initiatives.",""],[1,"13","1","Development Master Plans for Outer Islands and Rural Communities","The government in consultation with local communities has already formulated Development Master Plans for 'Eua, Vava'u and Ha'apai.",""],[1,"13","1","Pilot Community-Based Local Governance Model","Experience gained from a pilot community-based approach will guide the development of an appropriate local governing model and structure based on the principles of good governance.",""],[1,"13","1","Nuku'alofa Town Council Establishment","The establishment of the Nuku'alofa Town Council is coordinated by the Prime Minister's Office.","Prime Minister's Office"],[1,"13","2","Village District and Council Strengthening Programme","government will strengthen and support village districts and councils with the objective of giving communities a greater say in local development.",""],[1,"13","6","Community Development Small Grant Scheme","the government's structural reforms envisage strengthening good governance principles and committing funds directly for community development.",""],[1,"13","6","Community Development Project Financing for Vulnerable Groups","To date government has endorsed a small grant scheme anticipating to finance communities' development projects, many of which will benefit vulnerable groups in rural and outer island communities.",""],[1,"14","4","Youth Community Policing Engagement Initiative","This includes increasing the engagement of youth in community policing activities.",""]],"23":[[1,"7","5","National Infrastructure Investment Plan Implementation","Appropriate, well planned and maintained infrastructure that improves the everyday lives of the people and lowers the cost of business, by the adequate funding and implementation of the National Infrastructure Investment Plan (NIIP).",""],[1,"8","22","National Infrastructure Investment Plan Implementation","Appropriate, well planned and maintained infrastructure that improves the everyday lives of the people and lowers the cost of business, by the adequate funding and implementation of the National Infrastructure Investment Plan.",""],[1,"9","10","Sector-Wide Infrastructure Provision and Maintenance Approach","Taking a sector wide approach to the provision and maintenance of infrastructure, seeking alternative options for provision and cost recovery, and implement the proposed priority projects outlined in the NIIP (including: energy, telecoms, water, solid waste, roads, ports, airports)",""],[1,"18","5","National Infrastructure Investment Plan Implementation","Appropriate, well planned and maintained infrastructure that improves the everyday lives of the people and lowers the cost of business, by the adequate funding and implementation of the National Infrastructure Investment Plan.",""],[1,"18","13","Sector-Wide Infrastructure Provision and Maintenance Approach","Taking a sector-wide approach to the provision and maintenance of infrastructure, seeking alternative options for provision and cost-recovery, and implement the proposed priority",""]],"24":[[1,"16","5","International Peacekeeping Deployment Opportunities","It will also include seeking opportunities for Tonga Defence Service and Police Officers to serve in peacekeeping and similar missions internationally.",""]],"26":[[1,"17","1","Tourism Investment Promotion","Investment in tourism will provide new livelihood opportunities complementing those available in agriculture and fisheries in the rural areas; it has the potential to generate additional employment opportunities and increase foreign exchange earnings.",""],[1,"17","2","Tourism Investment Promotion and Partnership Support","Government will continue with and enhance the underpinning role it has in supporting this partnership.",""],[1,"17","2","Tourism Investment Facilitation and Destination Marketing Support","Government will continue to encourage investment in tourism by addressing issues and impediments to the industry as identified by the Ministry of Tourism and other stakeholders.","Ministry of Tourism"],[1,"17","2","High-Value Tourism and Resort Upgrading Investment","This means that substantial new investment in high-end resorts, where possible linked into the local community, and the upgrading of existing facilities will be needed.",""]],"27":[[1,"17","5","MAFFF Sector Development Plan","The government, through the Ministry of Agriculture and Food, Forests & Fisheries (MAFFF), has formulated the MAFFF sector plan that provides a coherent policy framework for promoting agriculture and food, forestry & fisheries development.","Ministry of Agriculture and Food, Forests & Fisheries (MAFFF)"],[1,"17","6","Private Sector Investment Promotion in Fisheries","These activities are planned to enable and attract private sector investment in the industry.",""]],"28":[[1,"7","14","Macroeconomic Environment and Fiscal Management Improvement","Improving the macro- economic environment and fiscal management, including effective revenue services to ensure a level playing field and those services to the people can be appropriately funded.",""],[1,"11","13","Tax Potential Review","Strategy 36: Undertaking a review of the tax potential of the economy.",""]],"29":[[1,"23","6","Constitutional and Political Reform Implementation","Implementing the Constitutional and Political reforms.",""],[1,"23","7","Anti-Corruption and Rule of Law Strengthening","Strengthening anti-corruption and the application of Rule of Law.",""],[1,"23","8","Electoral Reform and Election Boundaries Commission","Further work on political reform will continue, inter alia, under the Electoral Reform and Election Boundaries Commission.",""],[1,"23","8","Governance Efficiency and Accountability Improvement","the government acknowledges the need for continuing improvements in governance through more cost-effectiveness and efficiency in service delivery and by maintaining accountability and transparency.",""],[1,"24","2","Anti-Corruption Reduction Initiative","The government is therefore committed to minimizing corruption in Tongan society, and especially in, or in relation, to the public service and the operation of government itself.",""]],"30":[[1,"23","9","Government Structure Streamlining Review","Government will review the functions of the government structure to put in place a more streamlined system which focuses on the core functions and delivery of essential services, while operating within the viable levels of government revenue.",""],[1,"24","1","Economic Public Sector Reform Programme Continuation","The government continues the reform efforts made under the Economic Public Sector Reform Programme (EPSRP) to improve effectiveness in the provision of government services by focusing on three areas of public sector management - public administration, public financial management and public enterprise reform.",""],[1,"24","10","Public Sector Efficiency and Decentralization Reform","The government will continue the progress to a more efficient government through range of policies to ensure government focuses on its core functions, delegate to the relevant level of administration, and enables a greater role for the private sector and communities.",""],[1,"24","11","Administrative Decentralisation of Appropriate Activities","Decentralisation of appropriate activities to an appropriate level of administration.",""],[1,"25","1","Community Empowerment and Local Accountability Approach","This approach aims to enhance community empowerment, whereby local actors, capacities, and resources are mobilised for collective action to achieve public purposes.",""],[1,"25","2","Decentralization and Local Development Ownership Initiative","Government will also aim to enhance ownership of local development by local communities through engagement in more participatory approaches.",""],[1,"25","2","Skills and Resource Transfer for Local Communities","This will require appropriate allocation of skills and resources from the centre to help these communities.",""],[1,"25","7","Government Streamlining and Ministry Rationalization","there will be a concurrent emphasis on streamlining the government to focus on core services, while shedding functions that are not the proper purview of government.",""],[1,"32","8","Outer Island and Rural Development Program Improvement","Better formulation and implementation of outer island and rural development programs through local communities.",""],[1,"37","12","Public Sector Management Reform Programme","Continuing to implement public sector management reforms.",""],[1,"42","1","Economic System and Public Sector Reform","this would include in restructuring and reform of economic systems and the public sector to assist in making the economy more efficient and the provision of services more cost-effective.",""],[1,"42","3","Public Service Efficiency and Effectiveness Reform","The four enabling themes laid out by TSDF are targeting a more efficient and effective public service, more profitable public enterprises contributing, more dividends to government revenue and improving the effectiveness of revenue collection.",""]],"31":[[1,"26","6","Macroeconomic Environment and Fiscal Management Improvement","Improving the macro-economic environment and fiscal management, including effective revenue services to ensure a level playing field and that services to the people can be appropriately funded.",""],[1,"26","7","Prudent Budgeting and Public Financial Management Reform","Ensuring a prudent budget based on available revenue and a sustainable debt level, delivered through sound public financial management and quality government financial reporting.",""],[1,"26","8","Fiscal and Monetary Policy Coordination","Improving fiscal and monetary policy coordination.",""],[1,"27","3","Public Financial Management Reform","The Budget has to be implemented through a sound PFM so that Government can deliver services more effectively for the benefit of the population, and more effectively create the enabling environment under which the private sector can flourish.",""],[1,"27","3","Budget Execution and Transparency Strengthening","Core parts of the reform areas and work to be taken include the strengthening of the budget execution, transparency of the budget process, credibility of the budget, strengthened revenue efforts and improved quality of expenditure.",""],[1,"27","3","Public Expenditure Management Improvement","In continuing the process of strengthening of public expenditure management, government has been working with the Parliament Public and Finance Accounts Committee to improve public expenditure management, transparency and accountability.",""],[1,"27","3","Procurement Regulation Enforcement","It is also needed to strongly enforce and compliance with the Procurement Regulation 2010.",""],[1,"27","5","Regular Budget Reporting to Parliament","more regular budget reports to the Finance and Public Accounts Committee (FPAC) to increase parliamentary scrutiny of budget execution, in turn reinforcing efforts to strengthen the control of budget execution",""],[1,"27","6","Public Budget Reporting Transparency Initiative","making budget reports available to the public to increase the transparency of budget execution and the accountability of the government for its use of public resources",""],[1,"27","7","Public Release of Budget Proposal Documents","making documents such as the budget proposal available to the public when it is tabled in Parliament, to help clarify the distinction between what Cabinet proposes for the budget and what Parliament approves, and facilitate public scrutiny of the budget process",""],[1,"27","8","Public Tabling and Disclosure of Audit Reports","tabling the audited Annual Financial Statements and the Annual Reports of the Auditor-General in Parliament and making these documents available to the public to improve the transparency of the audit process and strengthen its effectiveness",""],[1,"27","9","Contingency Fund Operations Reform","modifying the operations of the Contingency Fund to avoid undermine the credibility of the budget, by avoiding the allocation of public resources to activities that have not been approved by Parliament during the year and are not unforeseen, urgent and vital",""],[1,"28","2","Government Bank Account Consolidation for Cash Management","consolidating the large number of government bank accounts to improvement cash Management",""],[1,"28","7","Medium-Term Fiscal Framework Development","developing a medium term fiscal framework for sound macro-economic planning and reallocation of expenditure priorities over time, and improvement in our debt position.",""],[1,"30","2","Budget Support and Reform Programme","Government recognises that budget support comes with reform conditions and is committed to work with development partners to develop and implement a programme of reforms consistent with the Vision of government",""],[1,"37","23","Prudent Budgeting and Public Financial Management Reform","Ensuring a prudent budget based on available revenue and sustainable debt level, delivered through sound public financial management and quality government financial reporting.",""],[1,"38","2","Fiscal and Monetary Policy Coordination Improvement","Improving fiscal and monetary policy coordination.",""],[1,"42","3","Whole-of-Government Donor Coordination Approach","government can provide more and improve services to the people and also more coordinated whole of government approach to donor assistance.",""],[1,"42","6","Development Assistance Mobilization and Budget Support","Government will continue to work closely with development partners to mobilize development assistance for development expenditure and capital investment, while making use of direct budget support over the medium term to avoid sharp cuts in government expenditure, while the economy and revenue base are set on a sounder footing.",""]],"32":[[1,"28","5","Tax Policy and Administration Review","undertaking a tax policy and administration review to assess the tax potential of the country and identify the level of revenue, and hence level of expenditure, that is consistent with an efficient economy and appropriate level of equity",""],[1,"28","8","Tax Potential Review","Undertaking a review of the tax potential of the economy.",""],[1,"28","9","Tax Reform and Modernisation Programme","Implementing tax reform and modernisation programmes to enhance revenue services and taxpayers' compliance.",""],[1,"28","10","Tax Compliance Enhancement","it becomes even more important that compliance with existing tax measures is enhanced.",""],[1,"28","11","Tax and Customs Reform and Modernisation Programme","The tax reform and modernisation programmes are still in progress; they concentrate on simplifying the tax and customs bases with clearly defined and modern procedures which will enhance revenue services.",""],[1,"28","12","Simplified and Transparent Tax Procedures Reform","The implementation of a simplified and transparent tax procedures, coupled with lower tax rates and easier filing of tax returns will help to reduce the burden on businesses and encourage both their growth and also international investment.",""],[1,"28","12","Trade Facilitation and Market Access Reform","Completion of these broader reforms will help businesses to get their goods to the Tongan market more easily.",""],[1,"28","13","Regular Tax System Review and Tax Education Programme","government will undertake regular reviews to gain a better understanding of the tax potential of the economy in order to ensure that the proper range and rates of taxes are applied to support government in the delivery of its services.",""],[1,"28","13","Educational Tax Programmes","Government will also conduct educational tax programmes to create an environment of",""],[1,"38","4","Tax Potential Review","Undertaking a review of the tax potential of the economy.",""],[1,"38","7","Tax Reform and Revenue Administration Modernization Program","Implementing tax reform and modernization programs to enhance revenue services and taxpayer's compliance.",""]],"33":[[1,"32","11","Gender Development Policy Implementation","Improving gender equality by implementing the government's gender development policy.",""],[1,"33","4","Youth Development Programs","by promoting youth development programs, including community economic development and the consideration of a National Youth",""],[1,"35","23","National Employment Register","National employment register [established and maintained]",""],[1,"40","7","Basic Needs Poverty Reduction and Youth Employment Efforts","we certainly need to step up our efforts in combating basic needs poverty, and provide employment, in particular for youth.",""],[1,"40","7","Gender Empowerment Measures","we still experience shortcomings in gender empowerment.",""]],"34":[[1,"33","22","Post-Harvest, Quarantine and Agro-Processing Facilities for Export Support","Post-harvest, quarantine and agro-processing facilities for export of local produce [established and maintained]",""]],"35":[[1,"34","23","Sector-Wide Infrastructure Provision and Maintenance Approach","Taking a sector wide approach to the provision and maintenance of infrastructure, seeking alternative options for provision and cost recovery, and implement the proposed priority projects outlined in the NIIP (including: energy, telecoms, water, solid waste, roads, ports, airports).",""]],"36":[[1,"36","19","Marine Resource Quota Enforcement","Enforcement of quotas to avoid over exploitation of marine resources [increased]",""]]}});